Title: THE KEEPERS
Credit: Written by
Author: Based on the History of Israel series
Draft date: April 13, 2026
Contact:
    Jon Wu
    captainjonwu@gmail.com

===

INT. TEMPLE MOUNT ARCHIVES - NIGHT - PRESENT DAY

A torch flickers against ancient stone walls. EZRA (late 20s, earnest, scholarly) descends worn steps into darkness, clutching a letter of introduction.

The chamber opens into a vast underground library — scrolls stacked floor to ceiling, maps carved into walls, portraits of forgotten faces.

                    MIRIAM (O.S.)
          Another seeker of forbidden knowledge.

MIRIAM THE KEEPER (ageless, knowing eyes) emerges from shadow.

                    MIRIAM (CONT'D)
          Tell me, child. Why do you wish to disturb 
          the archives?

                    EZRA
          I seek to understand how we survived. Every 
          empire that ruled this land fell to dust. 
          Yet we remain.

Miriam smiles, gestures at the vast chamber.

                    MIRIAM
          Look around you. This land has been Egypt's 
          highway, Assyria's prize, Babylon's gateway, 
          Persia's province, Greece's conquest, Rome's 
          burden.
          
She moves to a wall covered with ancient carved maps.

                    MIRIAM (CONT'D)
          Do you see the pattern?

Ezra studies trade routes, military paths, all converging on Jerusalem.

                    EZRA
          We sit at the crossroads of the world.

                    MIRIAM
          Precisely. While other nations could retreat 
          to mountains or islands, we had nowhere to 
          hide. Every conqueror's army marched through 
          our streets. Every empire's ideas collided in 
          our minds.

She pulls down a scroll showing the Fertile Crescent.

                    MIRIAM (CONT'D)
          What should have destroyed us instead forged 
          us into something unprecedented — a people 
          who could speak to any nation because we had 
          been shaped by them all.

                    EZRA
          Geography made us the world's crossroads.

                    MIRIAM
          But we chose to become the world's conscience.

She leads him deeper into the archives.

CUT TO:

INT. TEMPLE MOUNT ARCHIVES - SCROLL CHAMBER - NIGHT

Miriam shows Ezra a collection of identical scrolls, each bearing different seals — Babylonian, Persian, Greek, Roman.

                    MIRIAM
          Behold the secret weapon. The portable nation.

She unrolls one scroll — Hebrew text, detailed instructions for daily life.

                    MIRIAM (CONT'D)
          While other peoples carved their laws in stone 
          monuments that could be toppled, we wrote ours 
          on parchment. They could be rolled up and 
          carried anywhere.

                    EZRA
          But surely ideas alone cannot preserve a people?

                    MIRIAM
          These were not mere ideas. We created a complete 
          civilization in miniature — a nation that fit in 
          a bag.

She shows him scrolls from different eras, identical content.

                    MIRIAM (CONT'D)
          When Babylon fell, we packed up our entire 
          culture and moved to Persia. When Greece 
          conquered, we adapted their wisdom while keeping 
          our core. Rome could destroy our Temple...

She gestures at the vast archive around them.

                    MIRIAM (CONT'D)
          But they could not burn every copy of our 
          portable nation.

                    EZRA
          We became like water. Taking the shape of any 
          container while never losing our essence.

                    MIRIAM
          And in doing so, we discovered something 
          remarkable: ideas, when portable, become more 
          powerful than armies.

CUT TO:

INT. TEMPLE MOUNT ARCHIVES - MAP ROOM - NIGHT

A vast carved map dominates the chamber — not territories, but connections. Golden threads between distant cities.

                    MIRIAM
          You see networks where others see only exile.

Ezra traces the threads: Babylon, Alexandria, Cordoba, Kiev.

                    EZRA
          Rabbi Akiva in Caesarea could communicate with 
          scholars in Babylon faster than Caesar could 
          send messages to his own governors. How?

Miriam retrieves Hebrew letters from a cedar chest.

                    MIRIAM
          When Rome expelled Jews from one province, they 
          didn't just lose taxpayers. They lost their 
          connection to intelligence networks that spanned 
          continents.

She spreads the letters before him.

                    MIRIAM (CONT'D)
          These letters contain not just religious debates, 
          but grain prices from Egypt, silk routes from 
          China, political movements from Persia. While 
          empires built walls, your people built bridges.

                    EZRA
          The responsa. Legal questions about business 
          practices, but really—

                    MIRIAM
          Maps of power. When a rabbi in Spain answered a 
          legal question from a merchant in Baghdad, he 
          wasn't just clarifying religious law. He was 
          maintaining threads in a web that made the 
          Jewish people the nervous system of medieval 
          civilization.

Ezra feels the weight of this revelation.

                    EZRA
          To be connected to everyone means to truly 
          belong to no one. And yet to be essential to all.

                    MIRIAM
          Now you begin to understand.

CUT TO:

INT. TEMPLE MOUNT ARCHIVES - PORTRAIT GALLERY - NIGHT

A wall covered in portraits — faces in various court garments across centuries.

                    MIRIAM
          Behold the shadow ministers. While kings sat 
          on thrones, these advisors shaped the very 
          thoughts that moved empires.

Ezra studies the faces: a physician whispering to a caliph, a financier with an emperor, a scholar translating for a foreign court.

                    EZRA
          But why trust outsiders with such power?

                    MIRIAM
          Because outsiders owe their position entirely to 
          competence. Local nobles inherit influence. 
          Foreign advisors must earn it daily.

She touches one portrait tenderly.

                    MIRIAM (CONT'D)
          Rulers knew that these men's survival depended 
          entirely on their usefulness. A loyalty more 
          reliable than blood.

Ezra notices portraits changing hands across centuries — same families, different dynasties.

                    EZRA
          They became the permanent government. While 
          emperors were merely temporary occupants.

                    MIRIAM
          Now you begin to understand. But such power 
          comes with a price.

CUT TO:

INT. TEMPLE MOUNT ARCHIVES - ILLUMINATED MANUSCRIPT ROOM - NIGHT

Miriam unrolls an ancient manuscript — a robed figure whispering to a crowned king.

                    MIRIAM
          Here stands Mordechai, who saved a kingdom 
          through his wisdom.

She turns the page — a royal decree for destruction.

                    MIRIAM (CONT'D)
          And here, the same kingdom's decree calling for 
          his people's destruction.

                    EZRA
          How can the same person be both savior and 
          scapegoat?

                    MIRIAM
          The crown requires two things: competence to 
          maintain power, and innocence to preserve 
          reputation.

She closes the scroll gently.

                    MIRIAM (CONT'D)
          The Jewish advisor provides both. The skills to 
          solve impossible problems. And when those 
          problems persist, a convenient explanation that 
          preserves the king's divine image.

                    EZRA
          They wore the dual crown. Essential servants 
          who could never become kings themselves, yet 
          who bore the weight of kingly failures.

                    MIRIAM
          Prisoners of their own indispensability. To be 
          needed by power is to be owned by it. And to be 
          owned by power is to be expendable to it.

CUT TO:

INT. TEMPLE MOUNT ARCHIVES - DARKEST CHAMBER - NIGHT

Miriam arranges scrolls in complete darkness, reading by touch.

                    EZRA
          Why do you work in shadow?

                    MIRIAM
          Extinguish your lamp. Light reveals, but shadow 
          conceals. Which do you think has shaped more 
          kingdoms?

Ezra dims his flame. Miriam's voice continues from darkness.

                    MIRIAM (CONT'D)
          Here lies the record of Joseph, who never wore 
          Pharaoh's crown yet steered Egypt through 
          famine. Here, Mordecai, who remained a gatekeeper 
          while guiding an empire through Esther's lips.

Her voice drops to a whisper.

                    MIRIAM (CONT'D)
          And here — the hidden correspondence of advisors 
          whose names history forgot, but whose counsel 
          toppled dynasties.

                    EZRA
          But surely power means ruling openly.

Miriam strikes a match in the darkness.

                    MIRIAM
          This flame commands attention, blazes 
          brilliantly — and burns out quickly, leaving 
          only smoke.

She extinguishes the match.

                    MIRIAM (CONT'D)
          But darkness? Darkness endures. It outlasts 
          every light, embraces every corner. And when 
          new flames arise, darkness is already there, 
          ready to shape what they illuminate.

                    EZRA
          The greatest kings never sat on thrones.

                    MIRIAM
          The greatest power is the one that remains 
          forever unseen.

A beat of silence in the darkness.

                    EZRA
          So what happens now? I've learned your secrets. 
          Do I become a Keeper?

                    MIRIAM
          No, child. You become something more dangerous. 
          You become aware.

Distant footsteps echo from the stairwell above.

                    MIRIAM (CONT'D)
          Someone is coming. Someone who does not belong 
          here.

The footsteps grow louder, urgent.

CUT TO:

INT. TEMPLE MOUNT ARCHIVES - ENTRANCE CHAMBER - NIGHT

Three men in modern suits descend the stairs — DAVID COHEN (40s, Mossad operative), flanked by two agents.

                    COHEN
          Miriam! We need the archives. Now.

Miriam emerges from the shadows, Ezra behind her.

                    MIRIAM
          The archives are sealed to outsiders.

                    COHEN
          Not anymore. The Prime Minister has authorized 
          full access. We have a situation.

He throws a folder on the ancient table. Photographs spill out — diplomatic meetings, bank transfers, secret agreements.

                    COHEN (CONT'D)
          A shadow network. Controlling global finance. 
          Influencing governments. And someone is using 
          the old methods — our methods — against us.

Ezra picks up a photograph — a modern advisor whispering to a world leader.

                    EZRA
          The invisible hand.

                    COHEN
          Exactly. Except this time, they're not one of 
          ours. And they're playing a game that could 
          trigger World War III.

Miriam studies the photographs, her ancient eyes calculating.

                    MIRIAM
          You want the archives to find out who taught 
          them our secrets.

                    COHEN
          We need to know who the Keepers are now. And 
          whose side they're on.

Miriam exchanges a look with Ezra.

                    MIRIAM
          The archives hold many secrets. But some 
          secrets have guardians of their own.

She leads them deeper into the complex.

CUT TO:

INT. TEMPLE MOUNT ARCHIVES - RESTRICTED VAULT - NIGHT

An ornate door. Hebrew inscriptions. Miriam places her hand on the lock — it opens with ancient mechanisms.

Inside: modern technology alongside ancient scrolls. Computer servers humming next to 2000-year-old texts.

                    COHEN
          What the hell is this?

                    MIRIAM
          The evolution of the portable nation. You 
          thought we stopped keeping records in 1948?

She activates a computer terminal. Files appear — contemporary diplomatic cables, financial transactions, intelligence reports.

                    MIRIAM (CONT'D)
          We never stopped being the nervous system of 
          civilization. We just upgraded the infrastructure.

Ezra stares at the screen, understanding dawning.

                    EZRA
          Every major decision in the last century...

                    MIRIAM
          Passed through this room. Or rooms like it. In 
          New York, London, Moscow, Beijing.

Cohen's face hardens.

                    COHEN
          Who controls this network?

                    MIRIAM
          No one controls it. It exists as a living system. 
          Information flows where it's needed. Influence 
          applies where it's earned.

She pulls up a file — the same modern advisor from the photographs.

                    MIRIAM (CONT'D)
          Your threat? He's not using our methods against 
          you. He IS one of us. A rogue Keeper who decided 
          the old rules no longer apply.

                    COHEN
          Name.

                    MIRIAM
          Benjamin Weiss. Former protégé of mine. Brilliant, 
          ambitious, and convinced that the time for shadow 
          influence has ended. He wants to step into the 
          light.

                    EZRA
          The flame that burns out quickly.

                    MIRIAM
          Unless he changes the rules first. He's 
          orchestrating a global financial collapse to 
          force a new world order. One where the invisible 
          hands become visible rulers.

Cohen pulls out his phone.

                    COHEN
          Where is he?

                    MIRIAM
          Where all great games end. Jerusalem. He's coming 
          here, to the archives, to erase the old guard and 
          claim legitimacy as the new Keeper.

                    EZRA
          Then we need to stop him.

                    MIRIAM
          No. We need to remind him of the oldest lesson.

She gestures at the vast archive around them.

                    MIRIAM (CONT'D)
          True power dwells in shadow. The moment you step 
          into the light, you become a target.

INTERCUT — VARIOUS LOCATIONS AROUND THE WORLD

— Financial markets in chaos
— World leaders in emergency meetings
— Protests in major cities
— News reports of banking collapses

CUT TO:

EXT. TEMPLE MOUNT - NIGHT

A figure approaches in the darkness — BENJAMIN WEISS (50s, charismatic, dangerous). He carries a briefcase.

CUT TO:

INT. TEMPLE MOUNT ARCHIVES - RESTRICTED VAULT - NIGHT

Alarms sound. Miriam looks at the security feed.

                    MIRIAM
          He's here.

She turns to Ezra.

                    MIRIAM (CONT'D)
          You asked why I brought you to the archives 
          tonight. It wasn't chance. I needed someone to 
          carry the truth forward.

                    EZRA
          What truth?

                    MIRIAM
          That the greatest empire is the one no one knows 
          exists. And the greatest victory is the one where 
          no one knows there was a war.

She hands him a small data drive.

                    MIRIAM (CONT'D)
          Everything. Five thousand years of shadow influence. 
          Every network, every method, every Keeper. If 
          Benjamin takes this archive, he'll burn it to hide 
          his revolution. If Cohen takes it, Mossad will 
          weaponize it and start a real war.

                    EZRA
          And if I take it?

                    MIRIAM
          You hide it. You preserve it. And you wait for 
          the next seeker who asks the right questions.

Footsteps approach. Benjamin Weiss enters, flanked by his own armed team.

                    WEISS
          Miriam. Still guarding secrets in the dark.

                    MIRIAM
          Benjamin. Still seeking thrones you were never 
          meant to sit upon.

                    WEISS
          The world is changing. The age of invisible 
          influence is over. People want to see their 
          rulers, know their names, hold them accountable.

                    MIRIAM
          And be able to destroy them when convenient. 
          You've forgotten the dual crown.

                    WEISS
          I've transcended it.

He opens his briefcase — explosives, timed detonators.

                    WEISS (CONT'D)
          This archive ends tonight. The old ways end tonight. 
          And from the ashes, a new order begins. One where 
          we rule in the light.

Cohen and his agents draw weapons. Weiss's team does the same. Standoff.

                    COHEN
          You're not leaving here, Benjamin.

                    WEISS
          Neither are you.

He activates the timer — 10 minutes.

                    WEISS (CONT'D)
          The exits are rigged. This entire complex comes 
          down in ten minutes. You can try to defuse them, 
          or you can try to stop me. But you can't do both.

Miriam looks at Ezra, nods subtly. Ezra quietly slips the data drive into his pocket.

                    MIRIAM
          Benjamin, you're making the mistake every failed 
          Keeper has made. You think visibility equals power.

                    WEISS
          It worked for every empire in history.

                    MIRIAM
          And they all fell. We endured.

                    WEISS
          Because you hid. I'm done hiding.

                    MIRIAM
          Then you've already lost.

She presses a hidden button. The vault seals. Cohen's agents try the door — locked.

                    COHEN
          What did you do?

                    MIRIAM
          Saved the archives the only way possible. By 
          burying them again.

The lights flicker. Backup power activates — dim, atmospheric.

                    WEISS
          You'll die here with us.

                    MIRIAM
          I've been dead for centuries. What's another 
          night in the dark?

She looks at Ezra.

                    MIRIAM (CONT'D)
          There's one exit. Known only to the Keepers. 
          Through the water tunnels beneath the Mount.

She hands him an ancient key.

                    MIRIAM (CONT'D)
          Take what you've learned. Preserve what must be 
          preserved. And remember: the greatest power is 
          the one that remains forever unseen.

                    EZRA
          I won't leave you.

                    MIRIAM
          You must. The archives live in people now, not 
          places. You're the archive, Ezra. Go.

Timer: 7 minutes.

Cohen realizes what's happening.

                    COHEN
          The kid. He has the data.

Cohen and Weiss both turn to Ezra. Their teams raise weapons.

                    WEISS
          Give me the drive, boy. Last chance.

Ezra backs toward a dark corridor.

                    EZRA
          You both want to control it. Neither of you 
          understands what it is.

                    MIRIAM
          (to Ezra)
          Run. NOW.

Ezra runs. Gunfire erupts. He disappears into the darkness.

CUT TO:

INT. TEMPLE MOUNT ARCHIVES - WATER TUNNELS - NIGHT

Ezra runs through ancient passages, water rushing beneath his feet. Behind him: shouting, gunfire, chaos.

He reaches a junction. Uses Miriam's key on a hidden door.

CUT TO:

INT. TEMPLE MOUNT ARCHIVES - RESTRICTED VAULT - NIGHT

Cohen and Weiss face off. Their teams in a Mexican standoff.

                    COHEN
          Shut down the bombs. We can work this out.

                    WEISS
          There's nothing to work out. The old order ends 
          tonight.

                    MIRIAM
          (calm, knowing)
          The old order can't end, Benjamin. Because it 
          was never about buildings or technology. It's 
          about an idea.

Timer: 3 minutes.

                    WEISS
          Ideas can die.

                    MIRIAM
          Only if no one carries them forward. But ideas, 
          when portable, become more powerful than armies.

The lights flicker again. Miriam smiles in the darkness.

                    MIRIAM (CONT'D)
          You've spent your whole life learning our secrets, 
          Benjamin. But you never learned the most important 
          one: True power doesn't seek the throne. It whispers 
          to the one who sits upon it.

                    WEISS
          And when there are no more thrones?

                    MIRIAM
          There will always be thrones. Different names, 
          different forms. But the same game. The same 
          invisible hands.

Timer: 1 minute.

Cohen moves for the exit. Weiss blocks him.

                    WEISS
          We all burn together.

                    MIRIAM
          No, Benjamin. You burn alone. Because you stepped 
          into the light.

She presses another hidden button. A secret passage opens behind her.

                    MIRIAM (CONT'D)
          (to Cohen)
          Go. Tell your masters the archives are gone. 
          Tell them the Keepers vanished. Let them think 
          they've won.

Cohen hesitates, then runs for the passage. His agents follow.

Weiss stands alone with Miriam and his loyal team.

                    WEISS
          You're staying?

                    MIRIAM
          Someone has to keep the flame burning. Even if 
          it's only for a moment.

Timer: 10 seconds.

Miriam closes her eyes.

                    MIRIAM (CONT'D)
          Darkness endures, Benjamin. Remember that.

BOOM.

CUT TO:

EXT. KIDRON VALLEY - NIGHT

Ezra emerges from a hidden cave entrance, gasping. Behind him, muffled explosions. The ground shakes.

He looks back at the Temple Mount — no visible damage above ground, but he knows what's been lost below.

He clutches the data drive.

CUT TO:

INT. MOSSAD HEADQUARTERS - DIRECTOR'S OFFICE - DAY

Cohen briefs the DIRECTOR (60s, hard).

                    DIRECTOR
          The archives?

                    COHEN
          Destroyed. Weiss and Miriam both dead. No survivors.

                    DIRECTOR
          And the data?

                    COHEN
          Gone with them.

The Director studies him.

                    DIRECTOR
          You sure about that?

Beat.

                    COHEN
          There was a kid. A seeker. Miriam's student.

                    DIRECTOR
          Find him.

CUT TO:

INT. MODEST APARTMENT - JERUSALEM - DAY

Ezra sits at a laptop, the data drive connected. Files scrolling across the screen — thousands of years of hidden history.

He reads, absorbs, understands.

A knock at the door.

Ezra quickly disconnects the drive, hides it in a hollowed-out book.

He opens the door: SARAH (30s, sharp, beautiful).

                    SARAH
          Ezra? I'm Sarah. I was a student of Miriam's 
          too. Before you.

                    EZRA
          I wasn't aware she had other students.

                    SARAH
          The Keepers always have students. In case one 
          falls, another rises.

She enters, uninvited.

                    SARAH (CONT'D)
          She gave you something, didn't she? Before the 
          end.

Ezra says nothing.

                    SARAH (CONT'D)
          It's okay. I'm not here to take it. I'm here to 
          help you carry it forward.

                    EZRA
          How do I know you're who you say you are?

Sarah smiles, repeats Miriam's words:

                    SARAH
          True power dwells in shadow. The moment you step 
          into the light, you become a target.

Ezra's shoulders relax slightly.

                    SARAH (CONT'D)
          There are others. Across the world. Students, 
          Keepers, guardians. The network didn't die with 
          Miriam. It evolved.

She hands him a phone.

                    SARAH (CONT'D)
          When you're ready to learn what comes next, 
          use this. Someone will find you.

She moves to leave, pauses at the door.

                    SARAH (CONT'D)
          And Ezra? The greatest power is the one that 
          remains forever unseen. But don't mistake 
          invisibility for inaction. We shape the world 
          every day. We just don't sign our names.

She leaves.

Ezra looks at the phone, then at the hollowed book containing the drive.

CUT TO:

INT. MODEST APARTMENT - EZRA'S STUDY - NIGHT

Ezra writes in a journal — recording what he learned, documenting the methods, preserving the knowledge for the next seeker.

VOICEOVER (Ezra, older):

          "They taught me that geography shapes destiny, 
          but vision transforms geography into legacy. That 
          ideas, when portable, become more powerful than 
          armies. That true influence lies not in commanding 
          thrones, but in being the whispered counsel that 
          shapes the king's decisions.
          
          I learned that to be needed by power is to be owned 
          by it. And to be owned by power is to be expendable 
          to it. But I also learned that the greatest empire 
          is the one no one knows exists.
          
          The archives beneath the Temple Mount are gone. 
          But the knowledge survives. In data. In people. 
          In ideas that travel farther than armies and last 
          longer than empires.
          
          The Keepers endure. Not as rulers, but as guardians. 
          Not in the light, but in shadow. Where we've always 
          been. Where we'll always be.
          
          The invisible hand still guides the course of 
          nations. You just have to know where to look."

MONTAGE — AROUND THE WORLD:

— A young woman in London, studying ancient texts
— An old man in Shanghai, whispering to a business magnate
— A professor in New York, teaching history to eager students
— A financier in Dubai, moving markets with a phone call
— A rabbi in Moscow, counseling a government official

All connected. All part of the network. All Keepers of the flame.

FINAL IMAGE:

Ezra at his desk, writing. The hollowed book beside him. The data drive hidden inside. Knowledge preserved. Power protected.

The camera pulls back, through the window, into the night, over Jerusalem, until the city becomes just lights in the darkness.

And in that darkness, the invisible hands continue their ancient work.

FADE TO BLACK.

END.

---

## POST-CREDITS SCENE

INT. SWISS BANK - PRIVATE VAULT - DAY

A figure in shadow opens a safety deposit box. Inside: an identical data drive to Ezra's.

The figure removes it, plugs it into a laptop. The same files appear.

REVEAL: MIRIAM, older but alive, smiling.

                    MIRIAM
          (to herself)
          The greatest power is the one that remains 
          forever unseen.

She closes the laptop. Walks into shadow.

FADE TO BLACK.

FINAL TITLE CARD:

"The portable nation endures."

END CREDITS.
